From: lab0xy0 research
Subject: [PATCH] kbase: instrument the module for KCOV in in-tree builds

Instrumentation change, not a behaviour change. Discovery-profile only.

Arm's r54p0 defines MALI_KCOV only in midgard/Mconfig and its
-fsanitize-coverage flags only in the Android/SCons Makefile. An in-tree
build reads neither, and CONFIG_KCOV_INSTRUMENT_ALL does NOT cover loadable
modules: scripts/Makefile.lib:175 gates it behind $(is-kernel-object), which
is built-in objects only. The module therefore compiled with no coverage
instrumentation at all, and F-23 measured it: 2882 distinct PCs collected,
every one inside the vmlinux text range, zero inside the module range
(0xffffffffc0000000+). A coverage-guided fuzzer on such a kernel scores every
Kbase input identically while appearing healthy -- the failure mode this
repository exists to avoid.

Fix: opt the whole mali_kbase module into kbuild's own coverage mechanism by
setting KCOV_INSTRUMENT := y at the top of midgard/Kbuild, guarded on
CONFIG_KCOV so the baseline/kasan/debug profiles are untouched. With
KCOV_INSTRUMENT=y the module receives exactly the kernel's own CFLAGS_KCOV:

  -fsanitize-coverage=trace-pc              (always, with CONFIG_KCOV=y)
  -fsanitize-coverage=trace-cmp             (with CONFIG_KCOV_ENABLE_COMPARISONS=y)

This requires CONFIG_KCOV_ENABLE_COMPARISONS=y in the kcov profile fragment
in the same change: otherwise trace-cmp references (__sanitizer_cov_trace_cmp*)
land in a kernel whose kernel/kcov.c compiles them out, which is the modpost
"undefined!" failure class.

The guard matters for the other direction: CFLAGS_KCOV is non-empty whenever
the toolchain supports SANCov, so an unguarded KCOV_INSTRUMENT := y would
reference __sanitizer_cov_trace_pc in profiles built without CONFIG_KCOV
(baseline, kasan, debug) and fail those modposts.

Single placement at the top of midgard/Kbuild is sufficient because the
subdir Kbuilds are textually -included into this file, so one variable
assignment covers every object in mali_kbase-y.

Validated against: Linux 6.12.111 (x86_64), r54p0-01eac0 + the six
patches/virtual-device patches + 0001 (F-17). Acceptance is the falsifiable
criterion in TODO.md P6: a KCOV probe run must report PCs at or above
0xffffffffc0000000; a vmlinux-only pc_range is a FAILED result. See
analysis/findings.md F-2, F-23.
---
 .../kernel/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/Kbuild        | 16 ++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 16 insertions(+)

--- a/product/kernel/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/Kbuild
+++ b/product/kernel/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/Kbuild
@@ -215,4 +215,17 @@
 else
 # out-of-tree
     include $(INCLUDE_SUBDIR)
 endif
+
+# lab0xy0 research patch (findings F-2/F-23, TODO P6): opt the module into
+# KCOV instrumentation for in-tree builds. MALI_KCOV is unreachable here (it
+# exists only in Mconfig + the Android/SCons Makefile), and
+# CONFIG_KCOV_INSTRUMENT_ALL does not cover module objects
+# (scripts/Makefile.lib gates it behind $(is-kernel-object)).
+# Without this, the kcov profile collects vmlinux PCs only and is blind to
+# Kbase itself. Guarded on CONFIG_KCOV so the other three profiles are
+# untouched (an unguarded assignment would reference __sanitizer_cov_*
+# symbols that do not exist in a CONFIG_KCOV=n build).
+ifeq ($(CONFIG_KCOV),y)
+KCOV_INSTRUMENT := y
+endif
